### 🥎 12U Softball Pre-Game Itinerary (6:00 PM First Pitch)

**5:00 PM - 5:15 PM | Show Up & Settle In (The Mental Switch)**
*   **Arrival:** Players drop bags, switch to cleats, and get gear organized.
*   **The Switch:** Time to transition from ""school/home brain"" to ""softball brain."" 
*   **Coach Check-in:** Quick walk-around to ask about injuries, check the vibe, and make sure everyone has water.

---

**5:15 PM - 5:22 PM | Dynamic Warm-Up & Arm Care (7 mins)**
*We replace static stretching with movement. This elevates heart rates, lubricates joints, and creates mind-muscle connections to prevent injuries.*
*   **Dynamic Lines (5 mins):** Line up on the foul line. Jog down to a cone (approx. 45-60 ft) and back. Then perform: High knees, butt kicks, frankensteins (straight-leg kicks), walking lunges with a torso twist, open/close the gates (hips), side shuffles, and two 75% sprints.
*   **Arm Care (2 mins):** Arm circles (small to large, forward and back). *Trending:* If you have **J-Bands (Jaeger Bands)**, do a quick 2-minute band routine on the fence. It's the modern standard for shoulder health.

---

**5:22 PM - 5:30 PM | Intentional Throwing & ""Quick Catch"" (8 mins)**
*This isn't lazy, chatty catch. This is fast-paced, athletic throwing.*
*   **Progression (5 mins):** 
    *   *One-Knee / Two-Knee:* Isolate the arm action and wrist snaps.
    *   *Step and Throw / Long Toss:* Stretch the arms out by gradually backing up.
*   **Quick Catch Challenge (3 mins):** *Trending Drill:* Players pair up 30 feet apart. See how many clean catches/exchanges they can make in 60 seconds without dropping the ball. This works on footwork and lightning-fast glove-to-hand transfers. 

---

**5:30 PM - 5:40 PM | High-Energy Defensive Drills (10 mins)**
*Skip the traditional slow infield/outfield where 9 kids stand around watching 1 kid field a ball. Keep them moving.*
*   **Short Hops (3 mins):** Partners line up 10 feet apart throwing short, tough bounces to each other. Emphasize tracking the ball into the glove and fielding through the ball (forehand, backhand, and center). 
*   **The Star Drill (7 mins):** *A massive trend for building energy.* Players form a star/pentagon shape. The ball is thrown in a star pattern (e.g., Catcher -> SS -> 1B -> 3B -> 2B -> Catcher), with the player following their throw to the next position. It requires constant movement, extreme focus, and loud communication (""Ball!""). Once they get it down, add a second ball to increase the chaos and focus.

---

**5:40 PM - 5:52 PM | Pre-Game Hitting & Battery Warm-Up (12 mins)**
*Split the team. Keep groups small so they are getting reps, not waiting in line.*
*   **Pitchers & Catchers:** Head to the bullpen. Pitchers throw fastballs to get loose, spin their movement pitches (drops/changes), and end by facing 3 ""imaginary batters"" so they are mentally mid-game when the umpire yells ""Play Ball.""
*   **Hitting Stations:** Divide the rest into groups of 3-4 on pop-up nets.
    *   *Station A (Tees with Heavy Balls):* Focuses on driving *through* the core of the ball.
    *   *Station B (Rapid Front-Toss w/ Wiffles):* Coach or player tosses fast from behind a screen. Focus on timing, rhythm, and aggressive swings. 

---

**5:52 PM - 5:55 PM | Hydration & Final Prep (3 mins)**
*   Water break.
*   Catchers get fully geared up.
*   Final bathroom runs.
*   Players find calm and take deep breaths.

---

**5:55 PM - 6:00 PM | Pre-Game Huddle & Hype (5 mins)**
*   **Coach's Message:** Brief, positive, and focused on 1-2 goals (e.g., ""aggressive baserunning,"" ""loud bats"").
*   **Lineup:** Read the starting lineup and bench roles. Make sure everyone knows their job.
*   **Team Chant:** Captains lead a loud, high-energy team chant to set the tone.
*   **6:00 PM:** Sprint to your positions. Play ball!
